                "In parallel with valuation scoring, the DSP engine executes synchronized 'Budget Pacing and Frequency Capping Controls'. To prevent exhausting a client's daily $50,000 budget during the early morning hours, the bidding engine utilizes Proportional-Integral-Derivative (PID) feedback controllers that dynamically throttle bidding rates based on target hourly spend trajectories. Simultaneously, distributed bloom filters check the consumer's exposure history across the campaign to enforce statutory frequency caps (e.g., maximum 3 impressions per user per 24 hours), preventing ad fatigue and preserving media capital.",
